  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Similar to how Discord functions as a platform, you are able to share what song you are playing and \"Play\" or \"Liston Along\" when clicking on a user who has linked their Spotify.\n\nThe idea for the VRChat Integration would of course allow Spotify account linking. This would be different from the \"icons\" or profile links we have on our profile pages. Though if possible, I think we need a better socials link system. Last time I recall I don't ONLY have 3 socials... anyways another canny for another day. The idea is to link the Spotify account to your VRChat account (can't be steam or oculus). This would allow extra GUI options like:\n\n\"Spotify Profile Display\" - \"Display What you Listening to on Spotify in your profile Status! This will allow users to see what music you playing, as well as being able to play or listen along if you have Spotify Premium with a VRC+ Subscription.\" \n\n\"Hide Spotify Profile\" - \"This will prevent your Spotify Name or Profile from Displaying. If Spotify Profile Display is enabled, this will how Music Status Sharing alongside the ability to hide your profile name.\"\n\nI feel like this would prevent users from playing music via their mics and annoying others, when in reality now they can click on your profile and \"Liston Along\" and would also slow the OSC Spotify display scripts, allowing users to only see it when opening up the quick menu or open their profiles.",
